are permissively licensed (MIT/Apache-2.0/BSD/ISC/Zlib) and fetched through crates.io or pinned Git sources.
The craft-pdf writer and Krilla 0.8.2 backend are pinned to storytold/craft-libs revision
c3487320b2d1de657b860b3c8abb44e1f2b32bd8. The backend retains its MIT OR Apache-2.0 licensing
and upstream bundled material; see that revision's licenses/pdf-writer/ and ATTRIBUTION.md.
The backend patch prevents finalization during an unwind and rejects a writer after failed
cleanup. WordCraft enables only writing; PDF import and its image decoders are not enabled.

No Microsoft, Adobe, Avid or Autodesk icons, images, templates or artwork are included.

KhianKrub web-only font distribution
-----------------------------------
The web site distributes Sarabun (The Sarabun Project Authors, SIL Open Font
License 1.1) for its Thai interface. Original TH Sarabun New font files
(Copyright 2010-2011 SIPA; Suppakit Chalermlarp) use GPL-2.0-or-later with
the embedded document-font exception. Original TH SarabunPSK font files
(Copyright 2006 DIP and SIPA; Suppakit Chalermlarp) retain their embedded
Font Computer Program License Agreement, permitting unmodified redistribution.
The web site also distributes eight font families of the Thai Linux Working
Group (TLWG), version 0.7.4, exactly as TLWG publishes them: Garuda, Kinnari,
Laksaman, Loma, Norasi, Sawasdee and Umpush (GPL-2.0-or-later with the
document-font exception: a document that embeds the font is not covered by the
GPL) and Waree (Bitstream Vera licence; TLWG's changes are in the public
domain). The complete corresponding source release, fonts-tlwg-0.7.4.tar.xz
(also at https://github.com/tlwg/fonts-tlwg/releases/tag/v0.7.4), is
distributed beside the fonts.
All font files are separate, unmodified build inputs. The web fonts/ directory
contains their exact copyright/licence notices, full GPL text and checksums.
These files are not embedded into the native desktop binaries by this change.
